' SproutStudio: the classes that do the work in a project window, and what flows between them.
' AppGraph (manual DI) and the *Settings classes are left out on purpose.
' Arrow labels say WHAT goes across, not just "uses". Members are the real ones, trimmed.

@startuml dependencies
title SproutStudio · How a project window works
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
hide empty members
hide circle

package "Views (Compose)" #FFF8E8 {
  class Workspace <<view>>
  class CodeEditor <<view>>
}

package "ViewModels and state (Main thread)" #F1FBEF {
  class WorkspaceViewModel {
    root : File?
    docs : List<Document>
    activeIndex
    --
    save() · reformatCode()
    renameSymbol() · findInFiles()
  }
  class Document {
    value : TextFieldValue
    file · savedText · dirty
    --
    type() · undo() · redo()
    save()
  }
  class EditHistory {
    record() · undo() · redo()
  }
  class PreviewViewModel {
    image · problems · error
  }
  class GitViewModel {
    status · commitMessage
    --
    refresh() · commitSelected()
  }
  class SearchViewModel {
    query · result
  }
  class AutoSaver {
    watch() · flush()
  }
  class WorkspaceSession {
    reopen() · track()
  }
}

package "domain (pure, no IO)" #F4F4F4 {
  class SymbolIndex {
    occurrences · includes
    --
    usagesOf() · globalDeclaration()
  }
  class "CompletionEngine\nNavigation\nSymbolRename" as SymbolUsers
  class PlantUmlFormatter
}

package "services (IO, own threads)" #FFF1F1 {
  interface RenderService {
    problems(source)
    preview(request)
  }
  class LatestWinsQueue {
    submit(priority, key)
  }
  class DocumentStore {
    read() · write() · watch()
  }
  interface GitService
}

Workspace -down-> WorkspaceViewModel : reads state,\ncalls actions
Workspace -right-> CodeEditor : active tab
Workspace *-down- PreviewViewModel : one per\nvisible preview
CodeEditor -down-> Document : keystrokes -> type(),\nshortcuts -> value = ...

WorkspaceViewModel *-down- Document : one per tab
WorkspaceViewModel *-- GitViewModel
WorkspaceViewModel *-- SearchViewModel
WorkspaceViewModel --> AutoSaver : dirty tabs
WorkspaceViewModel *-- WorkspaceSession : tabs + cursors
WorkspaceViewModel --> PlantUmlFormatter : Alt+Cmd+L
WorkspaceViewModel --> SymbolUsers : Shift+F6 plan\n(off the UI thread)
CodeEditor --> SymbolUsers : completion,\nCmd+click

Document *-right- EditHistory : every write\nis a step
Document -down-> DocumentStore : save / reload

PreviewViewModel --> Document : watches text
PreviewViewModel -down-> RenderService : 300 ms after the\nlast keystroke
RenderService -right-> LatestWinsQueue : one PlantUML thread
AutoSaver --> Document : save() after 1 s idle
GitViewModel --> GitService : status, commit
SearchViewModel --> Document : unsaved text\nof open tabs
SymbolUsers -down-> SymbolIndex

note bottom of LatestWinsQueue
  A newer request with the same key
  replaces the one still waiting:
  fast typing never piles up renders.
end note

note bottom of DocumentStore
  The only writer to disk:
  atomic write, one lock per file.
end note

note bottom of SymbolIndex
  Declarations and uses of every name in one file.
  Completion, go to definition, find usages and
  rename all read it, so they always agree.
end note

note right of Document
  The model of a tab. Everything that
  changes the text goes through value /
  type(), so undo, autosave, preview and
  dirty marks follow without extra wiring.
end note
@enduml
